# snapdragon_policy_sync.fc
# Label the Layer-A headscale policy-sync agent binary as the entrypoint of
# snapdragon_policy_sync_t. The binary is copied to /usr/sbin by the
# (protected) build script; the OpenRC init (snapdragon-policy-sync) + the
# cron.d drop-in are baked alongside and installed (rc-update add) ONLY on the
# headscale control (pki) node by provision_headscale_policy_sync().
# provision_selinux()'s first-boot relabel (setfiles / restorecon -RF /)
# applies this.
#
# The registry cache it reads (/etc/snapdragon/registry/*) is labelled
# snapdragon_authkeys_cache_t by snapdragon_authkeys.fc. The rendered
# policy.hujson lives in /etc/headscale and stays etc_t in v1 (see the .te
# INFERRED-WIDE note — narrow to a headscale-specific type after the AVC pass
# if one is available).

/usr/sbin/gen-headscale-policy.sh    --    gen_context(system_u:object_r:snapdragon_policy_sync_exec_t,s0)
